=== April ===

* '''April 10th''' - '''Classic Egg Hunt Winner''' {{News/Playerworlds/Classic}}

Thor won the Classic Egg Hunt 2007 with an impressive 6666 eggs! As the winner he gained a Level 4 Bunny card for the new card game, 4 GC tickets, and his name down in the Hunting Hall Of Fame.

Congratulations to him, and thanks for everyone who took part.

* '''April 8th''' - '''Kingdoms Easter Events''' {{News/Graal_Kingdoms}}

The egg hunt on Graal Kingdoms started! You can either digg for regular eggs and then catch the jumping egg using a net, and then go into Hotaru gift shop to get one of the rare easter items. Or you can try to find one of the special eggs which  contain items like the demon shield or house renovation scrolls for expanding your house.

From time to time you will also see pink bunny lords invading the islands. The events team can now also hold special events where only certain weapons or magic are allowed.

Thanks to Stephen and Sayian for making the graphics for the new items!

* '''April 8th''' - '''Zone Easter''' {{News/Zone}}

Go the bunny in the dropship and get easter eggs (gives quite a lot of hitpoints) or buy a carrot dagger for stabbing your enemy! You will also see that some graphics have been slightly altered to match the easter look.

=== August ===
* '''August 28th''' - '''Computer Account Locking''' {{News/General}}
Graal has added a new feature that allows you to lock your account to a specific computer. If someone wants to connect to your account using a different computer then you will receive an e-mail where you need to click on a link to approve the new computer; This should make it harder to hack or steal accounts. To enable this protection, click on the "Protect" button in the serverlist screen.
* '''August 26th''' - '''Atlantis Relaunched''' {{News/Playerworlds/Atlantis}}
A new Atlantis has been released - with a story, quests and guides, a new interface and a completely new world with several islands which you can discover on your travel. The staff is also working on making the server available in English (default language is German). [[Image:Login_server_atlantis_new.png]]
* '''August 19th''' - '''Graal Skills Weekend Tournaments''' {{News/Skills}}
We were again holding several tournaments, and started the first tournaments for Gelats! The winners for the tournaments at this weekend are:
* Poker Gelat tournaments: Viper Vanduergan (ViperZakuto), Stefan * Poker big tournament: 1. Silver_Metal, 2. Storm Leonhart (StormYs), 3. MajinDragon *BomberMad: Marius (MegakuribohEXE), Zero (zokemon), Compulsar FairyNightmare (knightmare1) * Pool 8-Ball: Stefan * Pool Straight: Wolfey Xanadu (Wolfey)
Players were also hunting for highscores, here the scores of the best players: * Mahjongg: 86035 by Burn (dNeonb) * Marble Flip: 33795 by Burn (dNeonb) * Marble Maze: 2200 by Zero (zokemon) * Asteroids: 50560 by Burn (dNeonb) * Invaders X: 6220 by Burn (dNeonb)
* '''August 19th''' - '''Zone Metallic Rifle''' {{News/Zone}}
The traders sell a new weapon: the metallic rifle, which is shooting either a powerful 4-bullet shot (S-key), or a combo of 4 independent bullets which split on impact (D-key). It's not a rapid-fire rifle, but can be effective against groups of enemies or enemies hiding behind thin walls.
[[Image:Zone_metallicrifle.png]]
* '''August 18th''' - '''Zone Flame Bombs and Scifi Pistol''' {{News/Zone}}
New weapons have been added: the flame bomb which is a bottle that is thrown, explodes on impact and places some fire on the ground. The flame bombs are available from the traders. In the Shop window you can purchase a new pistol: the Scifi Pistol which is similar to the AP Ripper, but can also shoot sidewards when pressing the D-key, and has a higher fire rate in single pistol mode. We hope you enjoy the new weapons!
[[Image:Zone_newweapons.png]]
* '''August 18th''' - '''Zone Reapers Event''' {{News/Zone}}
This weekend on Saturday at 11 PM GMT + 1 (5 PM United States eastern time) a reaper will be given away on Zone by the events staff Crono (Gerami) . We hope that many players will show up and participate!
[[Image:Sayainreaps.png]]
* '''August 17th''' - '''Graal Skills Highscores''' {{News/Skills}}
We have added a highscore system on Graal Skill games, currently it is tracking the high scores for Mahjongg, Asteroids, Marble Flip and Marble Maze. You can watch the high scores by clicking on "All Games" or by clicking on the game, and scrolling down in the description window. This highscore is not displayed inside the game (Mahjongg sometimes says "new highscore" which is your personal score in the current game but not the online high score).
* '''August 14th''' - '''First Graal Kingdoms Poker Tournament''' {{News/Graal Kingdoms}}
Today we had the first Graal Kingdoms Poker Tournament. Everyone was invited to join the tournament with 1000 platinum coins. After 18 rounds we had a winner, sage_scooby won in a heads up against Ravenblade1979. Besides the money he also one an unique trophy with an engraving.
We are preparing more tournaments for Graal Kingdom prizes so stay tuned.
* '''August 12th''' - '''Graal Skills More Tournaments''' {{News/Skills}}
More tournaments were hold on the Graal Skills server, the winners are this time: * BomberMad: Stefan (of course!) * 8-Ball: Burn (Björn) * Poker: Ziro (xXZiroXx)
Next week we will do more events, we also plan tournaments for Graal Kingdoms items, so check out and prepare for more fun events!
* '''August 12th''' - '''Zone New Inventory''' {{News/Zone}}
We have added a new inventory using GUI controls. It can easier be navigated with mouse (left click for S weapon, right click for D weapon), but still works the same like the old inventory when controlled with keyboard. It offers more space for new weapons and its look can easily be customized using the new v5 GUI styles.
In the next few days we will release cool new weapons!
* '''August 11th''' - '''Graal Skills Tournament Winners''' {{News/Skills}}
Many players participated in the Graal Skills Tournaments, here the winners for Staturday: * BomberMad: Storm Leonhart (StormYs) * 8-Ball Pool Billiard: Storm Leonhart (StormYs) * Poker: Galapogos (Twinny)
More tournaments will come tomorrow!
* '''August 11th''' - '''Zone Event Weapon Match''' {{News/Zone}}
This Saturday, Anubis (Anubis_Wing) zone events team member hosted a prize event for blue pistoles. After a heated battle with the crossbow bolts flying every direction and gravitron bullets penetrating through barrels the winner was finally decided. The winner was Shadow (IXIs_Last_Stand) who won using the gravitron. Over 15 players participated in the event! Congrats to those who particpated! Next months event date will be announced shortly! [[Image:ShadowBP.PNG]]
* '''August 9th''' - '''Graal Skills Tournaments''' {{News/Skills}}
This weekend we will hold several free tournaments and tournaments where you can win Gelats - play Poker, Pool Billiard, BomberMad and more against other players! We have also improved the skill games to make the playing more fun:
* The game window is bigger, we removed the clouds-header * The tournament announcement PM leads you directly to the tournament list * When a tournament is added then a blinking link will appear in the Log window for easily joining the tournament * When inviting a player to a game then it is automatically selecting the best rule for the selected game (Bombermad: 3 Rounds) to make things easier * You can bet up to 50 gelats in Poker (might be increased later) * Nicknames are filtered (some special characters being removed) to avoid problems in multiplayer flash games * Easier navigation with keyboard: 'Space' starts a game, card games automatically select the first button in the start screen, when closing a game then it is automatically focussing the game list

=== February ===

* '''February 25th''' - '''Zone Chainsaws''' {{News/Zone}}
New item on zone: the chainsaw! You can win it in events and can use it for one hour to scare other players. We will hold several events for the chainsaw. Thanks to Sayian for drawing the chainsaw graphics!

[[Image:zone_screenshot_chainsaw.png]]

* '''February 21st''' - '''Graal X Updates''' {{News/Playerworlds/Graal_X}}
We have finished editing 1/3 of the main city, and is now accessible by the players. The gate is opened from 7 AM - 7 PM. When closed, you can go on the right side to pay for entry (5 dollars). This new part of the city includes an entire -full-featured- checkers game (for tournaments), motel's, a garage for cars (which you can reserve a spot in), and several stores, including a bagels store, a restraunt, a gas station, a radio station, and a post office.

* '''February 21st''' - '''Delteria Tournaments''' {{News/Playerworlds/Delteria}}
There have been revisions to Delteria's tournament schedule, check out our [[Worlds/Delteria#Tournaments|Tournaments]] page for more information.

* '''February 19th''' - '''Delteria Updates''' {{News/Playerworlds/Delteria}}

Questing has been re-enabled on the public overworld, the overworld has been made smaller, and two new quests have been added. See http://forums.graalonline.com/forums/showthread.php?t=72293 for more details.

* '''February 17th''' - '''Pixel Art Tournament 2007'''

Is pixeling your thing? Do you consider yourself a "pixel artist"? How does a free Graal subscription upgrade sound to you? Do you think you have what it takes to be the best of the best? If you answered yes to all these questions, check out the Graal Communication Forums for more information about the competition that is being hosted where you will go up against the best of Graal.

For more information, visit http://forums.graalonline.com/forums/showthread.php?p=1278632.

* '''February 14th''' - '''Graal Valentins Day'''
On several servers Graal players were receiving and giving presents to other players. On Graal Kingdoms events were hold where you could win love wands. On Zone the love rifle have been added which actually adds hitpoints when you shoot someone with it.

* '''February 4th''' - '''Kingdoms Events Display''' {{News/Graal_Kingdoms}}

On Graal Kingdoms the events that are managed by the Events Team are now displayed directly on the game window, you just need to click on a button that is displayed on the top of the window to see the event info and join it.

* '''February 3rd''' - '''Zone Freeze Tag''' {{News/Zone}}

The Zone Events Team can now host Freeze Tag events where the goal is to shoot other players using the ice cannon. Once a player is frozen he/she will be warped out of the game. 

The Events Team also got more commands to better control events, including a command to "soft ban" (prevent disturbing players from leaving dropships).

=== June ===

* '''June 24th''' - '''Ol' West 100$ Contest''' {{News/Playerworlds/Ol'West}}

In an effort to promote Ol' West, the server has set up a contest worth 100$ (USD). For more information click on the following link. [http://olwest.net/forums/showthread.php?tid=56&pid=263#pid263 100$ Ol West Challenge]

* '''June 9th''' - '''Kingdoms Fist Events''' {{News/Graal_Kingdoms}}

It is possible now to do fist-only battle events on Kingdoms. We have also fixed a problem with the escort quests.

* '''June 8th''' - '''Classic Monthly Spar''' {{News/Playerworlds/Classic}}

The Classic monthly spar for June will take place this Saturday, June 9th at 7pm EST.  Good luck to all those that enter. :D

* '''June 7th''' - '''New Management''' {{News/Playerworlds/Valikorlia}}

Valikorlia held a vote for the new manager. The results showed that Omake, an experienced staff member, won. He chose Setzer, another experienced staff member, as his co-manager. This update comes after, what players call, the failure of the previous manager.

=== October ===
* '''October 28th''' - '''Zone Medals''' {{News/Zone}}
Get medals for special achievements! We have added 7 medals which you get once reaching a special number of kills for certain weapons or doing special things. Find and get them all and show them in your profile!
[[Image:Zone_medals.png]]
* '''October 27th''' - '''Graaloween''' {{News/General}}
It's Graaloween time! Many servers are decorated with pumpkins and skulls and have released new weapons or monsters to celebrate Halloween. On Kingdoms you can enter the Halloween haunted house, and on Zone you can buy the popular ghost rifle and pumpkin rifles. Have fun!
[[Image:Halloweenmix.png]]
* '''October 21st''' - '''Kingdoms Battle Island''' {{News/Graal_Kingdoms}}
A new island has been added for kingdom battles. The entry to the island is marked on the map. The island is made for battles - you can even find a ship building place and monsters on it.
* '''October 21st''' - '''Zone Team Sounds''' {{News/Zone}}
The team sounds are now directly available in the item menu - you can easily map sounds to keys and activate them on the battle field to send messages to your team members. You see the icon of the head of the player on the left side of the screen. There is a filter to prevent mass sending of sounds.
[[Image:Screenshot_zonesounds.png]]
* '''October 20th''' - '''New Zone''' {{News/Zone}}
Many updates have been added on Zone: * New players can play without observer mode and can access more classes * More advantages for Gold players: you can assign hotkeys to weapons * You can play with mouse: shoot by left and right mouse key and cycle through hotkeyed weapons with mouse wheel
We will also hire an Asistant Administrator to bring more life into Zone.
* '''October 15th''' - '''Faded Nation's big move''' {{News/Playerworlds}}
After a lot of talk and preperations, Myself along with the rest of the FN management have finalized the move to Aeon. FN will now be the classic part of the 4 part Aeon world, formerly known as Elan; or now Elan, "The Faded Nation". We're excited about this and will try to bring you guys some of the best content of a classic world out there, thanks to Aeon administration for support on the move!
* '''October 15th''' - '''Graal Kingdoms New Parties''' {{News/Graal_Kingdoms}}
We have re-enabled several party commands like ''/party who'' and ''/party leave'', and the experience gain has been changed: no level gap anymore (any player can join the party) and the experience is shared based on each players level.
* '''October 14th''' - '''Era's Death Gui''' {{News/Playerworlds/Era}}
Once a player dies, there's a time to be revived. Before now, you couldn't see that timer. However, we've decided to release it!
[[Image:Era_deadbarpreview.png]]
* '''October 13th''' - '''Zone Planet Admins''' {{News/Zone}}
We have added several new commands for the Events Team to hire new events team members, and they can also hire planet admins:
* admin for only a single planet * can use only the commands for that planet * can kick and unstick players from that planet
This should make the events team more active. The planets are now also automatically reset when the events team members and planet admins logout, so that you can again use all weapons and the time for guild wars and deathmatch are correct.
* '''October 5th''' - '''Graal v5.11''' {{News/General}}
We have released a new Graal version:
* Video capture with compression * Fixed animated graphics (e.g. yoyo-shield) * New editor functions for text fields (auto-indenting, tab-spaces) like in the RemoteControl * Faster particle engine * Display of 3D objects on 2D servers * Auto-hiding of flash games when a PM or similar is shown above
Full feature list at [[Creation/Dev/Releases/Client/5.11|Changelog]].
* '''October 2nd''' - '''New Serverlist Icons and Fonts''' {{News/General}}
[[Image:newserverlist_small.png|left]] The Serverlist now uses the toon style by default (if you haven't selected another style). Also, new icons have been made for each server. It has been stated that if anyone wishes to make better ones, feel free to submit some by posting on the forums. New fonts have also been added.
